    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the undisputed anchor of the lineup. His elite 87.14 efficiency score is bolstered by a favorable matchup against the arm of Rhett Lowder (xERA 4.72) and a significant stolen base advantage derived from the starter\u2019s slow delivery. We are also leaning heavily into **Mickey Moniak**, whose 75.75 score is heavily inflated by a +14% park factor boost and a prime batting order position. While **Mickey Moniak** carries a 45% rain risk warning, his combination of power potential in a hitter-friendly environment and the platoon advantage makes him a must-start alongside **Gabriel Moreno**, who rounds out our top-three priority starts due to his favorable #3 spot in the order against a shaky 4.72 xERA rotation piece.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly rigorous regarding **Max Muncy**, who finished with a 48.80 score, narrowly missing the cutoff to start over our middle-infield options. While **Max Muncy** provided a decent floor, his projected #9 spot in the batting order created a drag on his overall efficiency compared to the higher-upside profiles of **Zach McKinstry** and **Travis Bazzana**. Similarly, while **Jose Caballero** represents our elite speed archetype, he was excluded entirely from the active roster\u2014registering a 39.32\u2014because the matchup against the dominant arm of Cease (xERA 2.94) coupled with a poor lineup position suppressed his value well below our mandatory 40.0 floor. We remain cautious with **Travis Bazzana** and **Mickey Moniak** given the weather volatility, but with **Corbin Carroll**, **Gabriel Moreno**, and **Brice Turang** locked in at the top, the offense is positioned to capitalize on the weak pitching staff facing us today.",
